From 1399eeaf6a9b2bd5248db5fa8f6a7fddeecda88d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julian Cooper <115541810+Juliansgith@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:12:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/52] Gate diagnostic probes behind /diag

The tree carries many temporary probes that log through Logf/Warnf/Debugf
with a bracketed tag ([STEERDIAG], [MOTDIAG], ...) -- some per unit per tick,
hundreds of thousands of lines a minute -- plus probes that append to
faf_diag.log and a mirror of every warning to OutputDebugStringA.

They are now dropped before formatting unless the game runs with /diag
(gpg::LogDiagnosticsEnabled, overridable with SetLogDiagnosticsEnabled). A
17-minute four-AI skirmish logs about 1,000 lines instead of about 936,000.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 31f5abbc4285f60aca6988514c4c73a8c2886ef3)
(cherry picked from commit 105e9d258c5d5ee362b0d7ac7adee23bfbc94c8e)

Ported onto 13ce9e55: upstream 5d68809b had already purged the faf_diag probes this commit gated in Sim.cpp, CUnitLoadUnits.cpp and CArmyLuaFunctionRegistrations.cpp (those hunks dropped); upstream's newer faf_diag.log probes (replay beat pipeline, silo assist, thrust, effects, Lua error mirrors, unit spawn, the sim-stall watchdog) are gated the same way.
